<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#rector-of-ragusa">Glossary</a> · Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rector of Ragusa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rector of the Republic of Ragusa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rector of Ragusa was the nominal head of state of the Republic of Ragusa (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>) from 1358 to 1808. Chosen from the patrician Great Council, he served for a single month and could not be re-elected for two years, living in the Rector's Palace and leaving it only on state business. The short term was designed to prevent any one noble from gaining personal power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rector-of-ragusa.jpg" alt="Rector of Ragusa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Ragusino at en.wikipedia · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rector%27s_palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
